WOW-BG3 vmangos patch 0024: a party is one WoW side, its owner's.

A party bot of another side than its owner (seen in play: Razor Hill's guards attacked an orc
hero's party for its Human Shadowheart; "keep race, take the faction of the main character") keeps its
race, class and quests and, while it is the owner's bot, borrows the owner's side: at its login (before it
is put on its map) and on every party tick, vmangos' Player::SetFactionForRace with the owner's race (team
and faction template), the owner's faction template itself (after `faction`, 0009), the owner's standing
and flags with every reputation faction (in memory), and the owner's forced reactions. Guards, towns,
attackability, PvP areas and the per-member feed's REACT then treat it as the owner. Its own reputation is
not saved over while it borrows; on its owner's side again it gets its own back. A bot of its owner's side
is left as it is. `.wowbg3 side MEMBER` (read only) answers `WOWBG3 side MEMBER RACE TEAM FACTION BORROWED`.

